# Flutter Mobile

Applies to Android and iOS alongside [Flutter](flutter.mdc), [Design system](mandatory-design.mdc), and [Interaction UX](interaction-ux.mdc).

- Respect platform safe areas, back behavior, system navigation, and touch target guidance. Keep primary controls reachable on phone and tablet layouts.
- Pick one owner for keyboard and bottom insets. Check sheets and pinned composers with the keyboard open and with supported Android gesture and three-button navigation.
- Verify permission prompts and denied, restricted, and revoked states. Route deep links through authenticated, authorized navigation and exercise warm and cold launch.
- Where used, verify push display, action routing, and failure handling on real devices. For Crashlytics or equivalent, verify the project's release configuration, symbol uploads, and crash delivery in a controlled test.
- Verify release signing, target configuration, permissions, and launch on affected devices. Keep signing keys and provisioning credentials out of the repository.
